A recommendation is a category-B-recommendation and is an evidence-type-4-recommendation.
If a clinician prescribes an opioid for a subacute-pain then the clinician should consider a testing-benefit and should consider a testing-risk.
If a clinician prescribes an opioid for a chronic-pain then the clinician should consider a testing-benefit and should consider a testing-risk.
A toxicology-testing can assess a prescribed-medication and can assess a prescribed-controlled-substance and can assess a nonprescribed-controlled-substance.
